window.EN={"1":"Roy and his group moved their army toward Juteaux, a city in the island's northwest, to save its people.","2":"Of the Western Isles, Juteaux was the largest city,","3":"and it housed the office of the Governor-General for the Kingdom of Etruria, which held this land as a protectorate.","4":"According to Elffin, the current Governor-General of the Western Isles, Arcard,","5":"was an Etrurian noble, but not much of a man.","6":"Etruria's reaction back home to an attack on the Western Isles' governor was a concern, but","7":"to save the island's people even a little sooner, he had to bring him down.","8":"Having resolved on this, Roy hurried the army on toward Juteaux.","9":"(Arcard): Hff, hff... Lord Flaer!","10":"(Flaer): Why, Lord Arcard...","11":"(Flaer): For someone who holds the post of Governor-General of Etruria's Western Isles, what has you so flustered?","12":"(Arcard): It's that accursed Lycian army!","13":"(Arcard): The Lycian Alliance's men are after me — they're closing in on this very office!","14":"(Flaer): Ah, you mean those people?","15":"(Flaer): To us in Bern, they're an irritating lot one way or another.","16":"(Flaer): At this critical time, I thought it troublesome for them to grow close with Etruria,","17":"(Flaer): so I had them driven out to this remote island...","18":"(Flaer): Hmm... they really are stronger fighters than I expected.","19":"(Arcard): This is no time to be impressed!","20":"(Arcard): Because of them, do you have any idea how much damage I've suffered!","21":"(Arcard): Ahh... the wealth I've built up on this island all this time...","22":"(Arcard): N-no, more importantly, my life! If they come, I'm finished!!","23":"(Arcard): What in the world should I do...","24":"(Flaer): If you're so worried, why not leave this to us","25":"(Flaer): and return home to Etruria?","26":"(Arcard): Is that all right?","27":"(Flaer): Fighting is what Bern's warriors do best — besides, we have a \"trump card.\"","28":"(Flaer): I'll be sure to finish off the Lycian Alliance's army for good.","29":"(Arcard): But...","30":"(Flaer): Lord Arcard... if we of Bern join hands with Etruria,","31":"(Flaer): there'll be nothing left in the world to fear. Wouldn't you agree?","32":"(Arcard): Y-yes, that's true... very well, I'll leave it to you!","33":"(Flaer): Hmph. How soft Etrurian nobles are.","34":"(Flaer): But once we've dealt with those Lycian Alliance people,","35":"(Flaer): these islands will be ours for the taking, Bern's alone... khe heh heh.","36":"※If you came through Chapter 10A and Chapter 11A","37":"(Roy): So this is the Etrurian governor's office... if we take it, we can go back to Lycia...","38":"(Elffin): Lord Roy, before we enter the castle, a moment.","39":"(Elffin): I heard a strange rumor in town.","40":"(Elffin): That there's \"someone who isn't human\" in the castle.","41":"(Roy): What do you suppose that means?","42":"(Elffin): The \"dragon\" sung of in legend... that it changes into a creature like that, or so they say...","43":"(Roy): !! A person? Turning into a dragon, you mean!?","44":"(Elffin): I don't know. In any case, let's proceed carefully.","45":"※If you came through Chapter 10B and Chapter 11B","46":"(Roy): So this is the Etrurian governor's office... if we take it, we can go back to Lycia...!","47":"(Elffin): ...My men should","48":"(Elffin): already be arranging things so we can get into the castle right away...","49":"(Elffin): There she is. That's the one.","50":"(Roy): Huh? The person dressed like a dancer?","51":"(Elffin): Yes.","52":"(Larum): Ah, Your Highness~!","53":"(Larum): Over here!","54":"(Larum): Over here, I say~!!","55":"(Roy): \"Your Highness\"?","56":"(Elffin): ...I wonder what she's talking about.","57":"(Larum): Oh my! You're so slow, Your Highness!!","58":"(Elffin): Larum, who is this \"Your Highness\" you speak of?","59":"(Larum): Eh... ah! N-no, um, well...","60":"(Larum): Mil... no, I mean, Lord Elffin just seems so princely,","61":"(Larum): so I came up with it myself — \"Your Highness,\" see!","62":"(Elffin): ...........","63":"(Roy): ...........","64":"(Elffin): ...Lord Roy, I apologize. Let me introduce you — this girl is Larum...","65":"(Larum): Are you Lord Roy?","66":"(Larum): The one no one in the Western Isles doesn't know of these days — Lycia's savior!!","67":"(Larum): Nice to meet you~ I'm Larum!","68":"(Roy): Eh! Wh— whoa! Please, keep your distance!!","69":"(Larum): Lord Roy! Your face is bright red — how cute~~~!!!","70":"(Elffin): ...Larum.","71":"(Larum): Ah! Th— that's right! This is serious!!","72":"(Larum): Everyone's been rumoring that there's \"someone who isn't human\" inside this castle!","73":"(Roy): \"Someone who isn't human\"?","74":"(Larum): That's right — they say it turns into some creature nobody's ever seen!","75":"(Larum): Some people are saying it might be like the \"dragon\" from the old legends!","76":"(Roy): !! A person? Turning into a dragon, you mean!?","77":"(Larum): I don't know, but... maybe so.","78":"(Elffin): Let's proceed with caution.","79":"(Flaer): Oh, you've come, Ein.","80":"(Ein): Wass... called... I heard...","81":"(Flaer): I'm going to report to Lord Narcian about the Lycian Alliance's army.","82":"(Flaer): While I'm gone, you defend the castle from those attacking it.","83":"(Ein): ...Understood.","84":"(Flaer): Hm!? Is someone there!?","85":"(Flaer): ...........","86":"(Flaer): Must be my imagination... well then, Ein, I leave it to you.","87":"(Ein): ...Understood.","88":"(Flaer): Kukuku, against this \"dragon,\" even the Lycian Alliance won't be able to do a thing.","89":"(Flaer): After all, it's hard enough to even scratch it with an ordinary weapon.","90":"(Flaer): The \"Dark Priestess,\" was it... His Majesty really has brought along an unfathomable monster.","91":"(Ray): ...So that's the truth behind \"someone who isn't human.\"","92":"(Ray): So it really was true that the Kingdom of Bern revived a \"dragon.\"","93":"(Ray): Sneaking in here was worth it, at least... now then, what should I do from here.","94":"(Ray): For a while, I suppose I'll pose as one of the soldiers here and watch the dragon's power up close.","95":"(Cath): I've co~me, all this way~ to the island at the western edge~","96":"(Cath): a rich mine, a people who suffer, and the governor's office ruling over it all","97":"(Cath): ...given all that, it'd be a crime not to find some treasure here.","98":"(Cath): It's not like the people here worked hard and saved it up themselves, anyway.","99":"(Cath): So I'll just help myself to plenty of it!","100":"(soldier): Word has come that reinforcements will arrive from the south soon!","101":"(Ein): ...........","102":"(soldier): ...Th— that's all. Excuse me.","103":"(soldier): Somehow... that guy's kind of creepy.","104":"(soldier): ...How's that cave coming along?","105":"(soldier): We hired some bandits and sealed off the entrance.","106":"(soldier): That should mean no one can get near the \"Divine Weapon\" anymore.","107":"(soldier): Good. Now all that's left is finishing off the Lycian Alliance army!","108":"(Chad): Whoa! Ray!? What are you doing here!?","109":"(Ray): That's what I should be asking you.","110":"(Ray): Why are you here? What happened to the orphanage?","111":"(Chad): ...You left without a word, and yet you're worried about it, huh.","112":"(Ray): It's not really that. I just thought of it when I saw your face.","113":"(Chad): ...The orphanage isn't there anymore.","114":"(Ray): What do you mean?","115":"(Chad): When Bern invaded Lycia, it got crushed.","116":"(Chad): The headmistress too... by Bern's soldiers...","117":"(Ray): !? The headmistress...","118":"(Chad): I'm going to avenge the headmistress. I'm stuck on this backwater island for now, but","119":"(Chad): someday I'll go back to the continent, and the day will surely come when I fight Bern.","120":"(Chad): When that day comes, for sure...!","121":"(Ray): ...........","122":"(Chad): Well, a story like this probably doesn't mean much to someone as cold-hearted as you.","123":"(Ray): ...I'll come along with you, too.","124":"(Chad): Eh!? You're serious?","125":"(Ray): Bern's army always has a \"dragon\" with it. I'm interested in that.","126":"(Chad): ...Fine by me, whatever. Just don't get in my way.","127":"(Lugh): Ray, it really is you! I wanted to see you!!","128":"(Ray): Lugh...! Why are you here?","129":"(Lugh): I'm glad, you look well.","130":"(Lugh): You just suddenly vanished, saying \"I'm off to train in magic,\" so...","131":"(Lugh): everyone was really worried about you.","132":"(Ray): ...Staying at that orphanage, I couldn't learn any decent magic anyway.","133":"(Ray): Well, that I managed to learn any magic at all in a place like that orphanage is practically a miracle.","134":"(Lugh): Ray... the orphanage isn't there anymore...","135":"(Ray): ? What happened?","136":"(Lugh): Bern's army attacked... they set it on fire... that's why.","137":"(Ray): ...Everyone else?","138":"(Lugh): The headmistress... protected us, and...","139":"(Lugh): the little ones are staying at Lycia's Elimine Church now.","140":"(Ray): ...I see, well, that's good then, isn't it — better than that poor orphanage.","141":"(Ray): The Elimine Church will give them a much better life.","142":"(Lugh): You don't... have to put it that way.","143":"(Ray): ...........","144":"(Lugh): Ray! Come with us, won't you!","145":"(Lugh): Let's beat Bern and go bring everyone back!","146":"(Ray): Sorry, but I'm not interested in something like that.","147":"(Lugh): But—!","148":"(Ray): Still... the Lycian Alliance might not be so bad. Seems to have some connection to that \"dragon.\"","149":"(Ray): If you insist that much, I suppose I'll tag along.","150":"(Lugh): Ray...","151":"(Ray): D-don't get the wrong idea!","152":"(Ray): It's got nothing to do with avenging the headmistress or anything like that!!","153":"(Lugh): Right! I understand.","154":"(Ray): So don't look at me like that!","155":"(Roy): Ah, wait a second!","156":"(Cath): Huh? ...What, it's you again?","157":"(Cath): You're always getting in my way — do you have some kind of grudge against me or something?","158":"(Roy): No, it's not that... it's just, well... I wanted to apologize.","159":"(Cath): Huh?","160":"(Roy): Last time, I... without knowing the circumstances, I said something like you were a \"horrible person\"...","161":"(Cath): Oh, that? I'm not bothered by it, really.","162":"(Roy): But still, I think what you're doing is wrong.","163":"(Cath): You, listen here...","164":"(Roy): So, won't you give me a chance?","165":"(Cath): A chance?","166":"(Roy): Once this war is over, I'll rebuild the land and villages ravaged by it, I promise.","167":"(Roy): To do that, I'll put to good use the crops and money I've been collecting from the people.","168":"(Roy): So, until then...","169":"(Cath): ...Hmph. And when's that supposed to be, exactly?","170":"(Roy): Once this war ends, though I can't say exactly when that'll be,","171":"(Cath): and you expect me to trust that and just wait?","172":"(Roy): Is that no good?","173":"(Cath): Why? Why are you saying this to me?","174":"(Cath): You could just leave me be, you know — someone like me.","175":"(Roy): If it weren't for you, we never would have escaped from that mansion.","176":"(Roy): Whatever your reasons were, you're the one who saved us.","177":"(Roy): I can't just leave someone who saved us be.","178":"(Cath): Good grief, at this rate you'll keep getting in my way wherever I go.","179":"(Roy): As long as you're somewhere along our path.","180":"(Cath): Fine, I get it. I'll stop coming to the battlefield to steal.","181":"(Roy): Really? Thank you, for understanding.","182":"(Cath): In exchange, I'm going to tag along with you all too.","183":"(Roy): Huh?","184":"(Cath): Talk's cheap — anyone can say anything they like.","185":"(Cath): I'll just have to watch closely and see if you can really do what you say.","186":"(Roy): Bring it on!","187":"Buuurn...","188":"Wh... at...","189":"(Roy): So this... is the power of a \"dragon\"... somehow we managed to beat it, but...","190":"(Elffin): \"Someone who isn't human\"... I see, so that's what it meant.","191":"(Roy): Bern... revived something like this...","192":"(Roy): ...just how many more \"dragons\" are out there?","193":"(Roy): Facing monsters like this, how are we even supposed to keep fighting!","194":"(Elffin): Lord Roy! Please, calm yourself.","195":"(Roy): Ah...","196":"(Elffin): ...I understand how you feel.","197":"(Elffin): But if you lose your composure, it will unsettle the whole army.","198":"(Elffin): Please, calm down...","199":"(Roy): ...I'm sorry.","200":"(Elffin): No, after fighting something like that, it's only natural.","201":"(Elffin): But with this, one truth has come to light.","202":"(Roy): A truth...?","203":"(Elffin): Do you remember?","204":"(Elffin): I told you there was a rumor that Arcard, Governor-General of the Western Isles,","205":"(Elffin): was pro-Bern.","206":"(Roy): Ah!!","207":"(Roy): For there to be a \"dragon\" in this governor's office set up by Etruria...","208":"(Elffin): It seems Arcard really was secretly in league with Bern.","209":"(Roy): Unbelievable...","210":"(Roy): If that's the case, then Lycia might be in danger — in any case, let's return to the continent at once.","211":"(Roy): We need to contact General Cecilia and figure out a countermeasure...","212":"※If you clear the map within 20 turns","213":"(Elffin): Lord Roy, before we return to the continent,","214":"(Elffin): there's something left undone here on this island of Fibernia.","215":"(Roy): Are there still enemies here?","216":"(Elffin): No, that's not it.","217":"(Elffin): A weapon we need in order to fight the \"dragons\"...","218":"(Elffin): one of the \"Divine Weapons\" is hidden in a nearby cave.","219":"(Elffin): If we could get our hands on it, the fight against the \"dragons\" would surely be easier...","220":"(Roy): A \"Divine Weapon\"... a weapon used by the \"Eight Legends\" to defeat \"dragons.\"","221":"(Roy): I see! If we gather those, we'll have a chance against Bern!","222":"(Elffin): Yes. There are eight \"Divine Weapons\" in all...","223":"(Elffin): the more we manage to obtain, the more it will favor us in the fight.","224":"(Roy): All right, let's head to that cave at once!","225":"※If you clear the map on turn 21 or later","226":"(soldier): T— terrible news!! Word has just come from Etruria...","227":"(soldier): There's been a coup d'état in the royal capital, Aquleia!","228":"(Marinus): Wh— what did you say!","229":"(soldier): The masterminds behind the coup are Chancellor Roartz and Arcard, Governor-General of the Western Isles.","230":"(soldier): With those two at its center, the coup faction first captured King Mordred,","231":"(soldier): and has declared that, together with the Kingdom of Bern, they will divide the world between them!","232":"(Marinus): This can't be happening...","233":"(Marinus): So... Etruria and Bern — the continent's two great kingdoms — have joined hands...","234":"(Roy): Lady Cecili— no, General Cecilia, is she safe!?","235":"(Roy): And... what of Princess Guinivere...?","236":"(soldier): We don't know the details, but...","237":"(soldier): Etruria's \"Three Generals,\" who oversee its military affairs,","238":"(soldier): it seems they too have split apart.","239":"(soldier): General Cecilia of the Mage Corps got word beforehand and narrowly escaped the capital,","240":"(soldier): and is said to be heading for the Misur Peninsula at the continent's western edge.","241":"(Roy): And the remaining generals?","242":"(soldier): With the King held hostage, they've sided with the coup faction, it seems.","243":"(Marinus): Lord Roy...","244":"(Roy): In any case, let's get in touch with Cecilia.","245":"(Roy): Cecilia... Princess Guinivere... both of you... please, be safe!"};
